<%# The free-delivery countdown, refreshed by turbo_stream whenever the cart
    changes (see cart_items/*.turbo_stream.erb). Rendered server-side from the
    one helper so the sentence cannot drift between its initial render and its
    replacements, and so the arithmetic lives next to the rule it mirrors.

    Treated as a status band rather than another line of grey copy: it is the
    only thing under the button that CHANGES as the buyer shops, and sitting at
    the same weight as the static trust and sample blocks below made it read as
    the first line of that stack.

    The band shows PROGRESS, not just a sentence. A nudge whose only content is
    a number asks the buyer to hold the threshold in their head to know whether
    £43.96 is nearly there or nowhere near; the bar answers that at a glance,
    and it visibly moves as the cart grows, which is the thing a countdown is
    for. The tint tracks state on top of it, so closing the gap reads without
    being read.

    Mounted on the PDP buy box, in the cart drawer and in the cart page's
    summary column; the stream replacements are harmless no-ops on pages that do
    not carry it.

    `id` exists because two of those surfaces share a document: the drawer is
    mounted on the PDP (and on every shop, collection and category page), so a
    fixed id would put two copies of it under one name and leave the streams
    replacing an arbitrary one. The buy box keeps the original
    `free_delivery_hint`, since the streams that target it by name are already
    deployed; the cart surfaces pass their own. %>
<% dom_id = local_assigns.fetch(:id, "free_delivery_hint") %>
<%# The band's own spacing belongs to the surface around it, not to the band:
    mt-5 is the gap under the buy box's button, and the cart surfaces sit it
    against a totals block instead. %>
<% spacing = local_assigns.fetch(:spacing, "mt-5") %>
<% subtotal = Current.cart&.subtotal_amount || 0 %>
<% qualified = free_delivery_qualified?(subtotal) %>
<% progress = free_delivery_progress(subtotal) %>
<%# An empty cart has no spend to plot, so it gets the promise alone: a bar
    pinned at zero under "orders over £100" states a starting line nobody has
    crossed yet, which is discouraging rather than motivating. %>
<% show_bar = subtotal.to_d.positive? %>
<div id="<%= dom_id %>"
     data-test="free-delivery-hint"
     data-qualified="<%= qualified %>"
     data-progress="<%= progress %>"
     class="<%= spacing %> rounded-xl border px-4 py-3.5
            <%= qualified ? "border-success/40 bg-success/10" : "border-base-300 bg-base-200" %>">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
    <%# The icon sits in its own tinted tile rather than floating beside the
        sentence. At icon size alone it read as stranded next to a label that
        wraps to two lines, having nothing to align to; the tile gives it a
        shape of its own and anchors the row. %>
    <span class="flex h-9 w-9 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg
                 <%= qualified ? "bg-success/25 text-success-content" : "bg-success/15 text-success-content" %>">
      <% if qualified %>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/>
        </svg>
      <% else %>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 17a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0zm10 0a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0zM3 4h2l2 11h11l2-7H7"/>
        </svg>
      <% end %>
    </span>

    <%# The money figure carries the emphasis: it is the part a buyer scans for,
        whether it is the threshold or the gap left to close. Left-aligned, so a
        sentence that wraps stacks against the tile instead of centring itself
        into a ragged block. %>
    <span class="text-left text-base leading-snug"><%= highlight_money(free_delivery_nudge(subtotal)) %></span>
  </div>

  <% if show_bar %>
    <%# A native <progress>: the fill is set by value/max, so the width needs no
        inline style (the project forbids them) and the element carries its own
        meaning for assistive tech. aria-label rather than a visible label,
        because the sentence above already says what it measures. %>
    <progress class="progress progress-success mt-3 h-1.5 w-full bg-base-300"
              value="<%= progress %>"
              max="100"
              aria-label="Progress toward free mainland UK delivery"
              data-test="free-delivery-progress"></progress>

    <% unless qualified %>
      <%# The bar's anchors. Without them the fill is an impression rather than
          a measure: these say what has been spent and what it is being measured
          against. Dropped once qualified, where the bar is full and the
          threshold has stopped being the point. %>
      <div class="mt-1.5 flex justify-between text-xs text-gray-500">
        <span data-test="free-delivery-spent"><%= number_to_currency(subtotal) %></span>
        <span><%= free_shipping_threshold_display %></span>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
